<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Ostrogothic Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">493 CE – 553 CE · capital Ravenna</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Gothic kingdom of Theodoric the Great in Italy, which preserved Roman government and culture before Justinian's armies destroyed it.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ostrogoths">Ostrogoths</a>, settled in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a> as federates of the eastern empire, were sent to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> by the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeno-emperor">Zeno</a> under their king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodoric-the-great">Theodoric</a>. They invaded in 489, besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odoacer">Odoacer</a> in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-ravenna">Ravenna</a> and killed him in 493, and Theodoric became ruler of Italy under nominal imperial authority.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodoric-the-great">Theodoric</a> governed through Roman officials and the Senate, while the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goths">Goths</a> formed the army and kept their Arian faith. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cassiodorus">Cassiodorus</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boethius">Boethius</a> served him, though he executed Boethius in 524. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-ravenna">Ravenna</a> gained <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santapollinare-nuovo">Sant'Apollinare Nuovo</a> and his mausoleum. His realm reached into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-provence">Provence</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmatia">Dalmatia</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a>, and he led a network of Germanic kingdoms through marriage alliances.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodoric-the-great">Theodoric</a>'s death in 526, the murder of his daughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amalasuntha">Amalasuntha</a> gave Justinian a pretext to invade in 535. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belisarius">Belisarius</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narses">Narses</a> fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goths">Goths</a> for almost twenty years, leaving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> devastated. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/totila">Totila</a> was killed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-taginae">Busta Gallorum</a> in 552, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teia">Teia</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mons-lactarius">Mons Lactarius</a> in 552 or 553.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/ostrogothic-kingdom.jpg" alt="Ostrogothic Kingdom" width="320" height="320"><figcaption>Image: [1] · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Teodorico_re_dei_Goti_(493-526)_white.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>493 CE – 553 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ravenna</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Theodoric the Great, Amalasuntha, Totila</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Arian Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gothic, Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a>, <a href="/countries/slovenia">Slovenia</a>, <a href="/countries/croatia">Croatia</a>, <a href="/countries/austria">Austria</a>, <a href="/countries/switzerland">Switzerland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of the Ostrogoths, Kingdom of Italy (Ostrogothic)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=523&amp;focus=ostrogothic-kingdom" aria-label="Ostrogothic Kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4972 607 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ostrogothic Kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5292 863L5292 863M5292 863L5709 970M5292 863L5035 888"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5292 863h0M5709 970h0M5035 888h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5292 863h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5292 863h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Ravenna. <a href="/atlas?year=523&amp;focus=ostrogothic-kingdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
